GitHub Issue:
Post Date: 2020-02-04T14:31:33Z
Current Date: April 4 2025
Title: Get GraphQL Schema when using GraphType First
Description: We are building our api using a GraphType first approach, however it would be useful to be able to export this to a GraphQL schema as this is easier to discuss with others. I cannot find any documentation or obvious methods that seem to allow me to do this. Am I missing it or is this not possible currently?

For example, I was hoping to be able to do something like:
```
using System;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using GraphQL;
using GraphQL.Types;

public class Droid
{
  public string Id { get; set; }
  public string Name { get; set; }
}

public class DroidType : ObjectGraphType<Droid>
{
  public DroidType()
  {
    Field(x => x.Id).Description("The Id of the Droid.");
    Field(x => x.Name).Description("The name of the Droid.");
  }
}

public class StarWarsQuery : ObjectGraphType
{
  public StarWarsQuery()
  {
    Field<DroidType>(
      "hero",
      resolve: context => new Droid { Id = "1", Name = "R2-D2" }
    );
  }
}

public class Program
{
  public static async Task Main(string[] args)
  {
    var schema = new Schema { Query = new StarWarsQuery() };

    var gqlSchema = await schema.ToGraphQLSchema();

    Console.WriteLine(gqlSchema);
  }
}
```

Which would give:
```
type Droid {
    id: String!
    name: String!
  }

  type Query {
    hero: Droid
  }
```

